  "details": "Adding an interactive in-world menu to the hub would greatly add to the immersion of that world. It would create a reason for players to travel there as well as creating a point of interest.  As mentioned in another post, these settings would be better off not in the players menu as it would be far too easy to make a mistake.  \n\n\nPossible Use Cases:\n\nEvent Calendar:\n\tWhile the current implementation of the event works, it is more of a shout-out rather than a notification.  This would add a location in game where players could go to explore community events in a more cohesive manner.  There would be a menu where players could select a date and see a list of events taking place on that day.  This could create a much more direct means of informing users of upcoming events. \nIn addition, players could have the ability to set up or propose events of their own from this interface.  Obviously certain restrictions, such as mod approval, would need to be put in place in order to minimise spam and other transgressions.  In addition, as events these days have gotten rather crowded, these events could be made to pertain to certain friend groups or invited members.  \n\nMaking Worlds Public:\n\tThis could add an interface through which a user could submit a request to make a world public.  The options would be pulled from a users “uploaded worlds list”.  In addition, players could use this as a means to change settings on their worlds, such as making an already public world private.\n\nWorlds Map:\n\tTouch a location, spawn a portal to that world.  (Something something treasure planet…)\n\nSubmit an Avatar for “Featured Avatar”\n\t-\n\nServer Status and Information (Like what is on discord but more centralized)\n\nSubhub Settings:  \n(https://vrchat.canny.io/feature-requests/p/structural-idea-subhubs)",
